# Source preparation pipeline to be run from mapterhorn/pipelines folder.
# Real (non-trial) coverage for the growing Kyushu/Okinawa 1m dataset --
# originally created 2026-08-10 as a throwaway end-to-end pipeline
# speed-validation source for the aalto->slate migration (see
# HANDOVER.md), then repurposed the same day into the real bridge
# source-catalog entry for this region, per Hidenori's own "no strong
# reason not to let it become the real entry" call -- kept the
# jpnational1 name to avoid re-downloading under a new name.
#
# Not geographically cropped -- covers every mesh position published
# under smartmaps/japan-geotiff-dem/1/ whose 1st-level JIS mesh code
# falls in the empirically-confirmed Kyushu/Okinawa range 3900-5199
# (vs. Hokkaido's 6100-6899). 71,577 unique positions as of this
# writing, deduplicated by keeping only the newest survey date per
# position (SC's sync is additive-only; multiple dates coexist for the
# same mesh -- same dedup logic as jpshakotan1/jphakodatecity1, see
# DECISIONS.md). Only 49 of the 71,577 positions reflect the current
# 2026-06-03 Kyushu/Okinawa DEM1A refresh so far -- the rest are older
# (pre-refresh) survey dates; file_list.txt will need periodic
# regeneration as more of the refresh lands on Source Cooperative and
# gets synced (see japan-geotiff-dem's own HANDOVER.md for that
# pipeline's progress).
#
# No 5m/10m fallback entry built yet for this region (unlike
# jphakodatecity5m/10m, jpsapporo5m/10m, jpshakotan5m/10m) -- deferred
# given the much larger scale here; expect 1m-only coverage gaps at
# this pass. No sea-crop entry either (c.f. jphakodatetrialsea,
# jpsapporosea, jpshakotansea) -- same reasoning, follow-up work.
# source_to_cog.py deliberately skipped, same reasoning as jpsapporo1.
[no-cd]
default:
    uv run python source_download.py jpnational1
    uv run python source_bounds.py jpnational1
    uv run python source_polygonize.py jpnational1 4
